Keep a shared starts as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into starts.
Place 2 into starts.
Place 4 into starts.
Place 5 into starts.
Place 6 into starts.
Keep a shared parents as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into parents.
Place 1 into parents.
Place 2 into parents.
Place 3 into parents.
Keep a shared rootresult as 0.
Keep a shared sharedfound as 0.
Keep a shared gathered as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared merged as empty text.
Keep a shared candidate as empty text.
Keep a shared found as 0.

To root from node (a whole number).
If item node of parents is node, set rootresult to node, return.
Root from item node of parents.

To merge from first (a whole number) with second (a whole number).
Root from first.
The firstroot is rootresult.
Root from second.
The secondroot is rootresult.
If firstroot is not secondroot, set item firstroot of parents to secondroot.

To share from first (a whole number) with second (a whole number).
Set sharedfound to 0.
For every left from item first of starts to item (first plus 1) of starts minus 1.
For every right from item second of starts to item (second plus 1) of starts minus 1.
If item left of emails matches item right of emails, set sharedfound to 1.

To locate from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than the last position of gathered, return.
If item spot of gathered matches candidate, set found to 1, return.
Locate from spot plus 1.

To gather from person (a whole number) with root (a whole number).
Root from person.
If rootresult is not root, return.
For every spot from item person of starts to item (person plus 1) of starts minus 1.
Set candidate to item spot of emails.
Set found to 0.
Locate from 0.
If found is 0, Place candidate into gathered.

To order.
The total is the number of items in gathered.
The final is total minus 1.
For every left from 0 to final.
For every right from left plus 1 to final.
If item right of gathered comes before item left of gathered, swap item left of gathered and item right of gathered.

To attach from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than the last position of gathered, return.
Place "," into merged.
Place item spot of gathered into merged.
Attach from spot plus 1.

To wipe.
The count is the number of items in gathered.
If count is 0, return.
Remove the last item from gathered.
Wipe.

To render from person (a whole number) with root (a whole number).
Wipe.
For every member from 0 to the last position of people, Gather from member with root.
Order.
The source is item person of people.
Set merged to a copy of source.
Attach from 0.
Show merged.

For every left from 0 to the last position of people.
For every right from left plus 1 to the last position of people.
Share from left with right.
If sharedfound is 1, merge from left with right.

For every person from 0 to the last position of people.
Root from person.
If rootresult is person, Render from person with person.

